PVST+ — Cisco's STP Version

Cisco switches run PVST+ (Per-VLAN Spanning Tree Plus) by default
Runs a separate STP instance for each VLAN
Allows different Root Bridges per VLAN for load balancing
Modern switches default to Rapid-PVST+ (Day 22)

STP mode commands:
spanning-tree mode pvst          ! Classic 802.1D per VLAN
spanning-tree mode rapid-pvst    ! Rapid STP — default on modern switches

STP Configuration Commands
Configuring the Root Bridge:
spanning-tree vlan 1 priority 4096        ! Manual (must be multiple of 4096)
spanning-tree vlan 1 root primary         ! Macro: sets to 24576 or lower
spanning-tree vlan 1 root secondary       ! Sets priority to 28672
Port cost and priority:
interface g0/1
  spanning-tree vlan 1 cost 10
  spanning-tree vlan 1 port-priority 64
Verification:
show spanning-tree
show spanning-tree vlan 1
show spanning-tree interface g0/1 detail

STP Load Balancing
! SW1: Root for VLAN 1, secondary for VLAN 2
spanning-tree vlan 1 root primary
spanning-tree vlan 2 root secondary

! SW2: Root for VLAN 2, secondary for VLAN 1
spanning-tree vlan 2 root primary
spanning-tree vlan 1 root secondary

STP Toolkit
1. PortFast
Bypasses Listening and Learning — port goes directly to Forwarding.
Use on access ports connected to end hosts. NEVER on switch-to-switch ports.
interface g0/1
  spanning-tree portfast

spanning-tree portfast default   ! Enable globally on all access ports
2. BPDU Guard
Shuts port into err-disabled if a BPDU is received on a PortFast port.
Always pair with PortFast.
interface g0/1
  spanning-tree bpduguard enable

spanning-tree portfast bpduguard default   ! Enable globally

errdisable recovery cause bpduguard        ! Auto-recover
errdisable recovery interval 30
3. BPDU Filter
Stops a port from sending or receiving BPDUs. Use carefully — can cause loops.
spanning-tree portfast bpdufilter default  ! Global (safer)

interface g0/1
  spanning-tree bpdufilter enable          ! Per-interface (disables STP — dangerous)
4. Root Guard
Blocks port (root-inconsistent) if a superior BPDU is received.
Use on Designated Ports facing downstream switches.
interface g0/1
  spanning-tree guard root
5. Loop Guard
Blocks port (loop-inconsistent) if BPDUs stop being received.
Auto-recovers when BPDUs resume. Use on Root Ports and Non-Designated Ports.
interface g0/1
  spanning-tree guard loop

spanning-tree loopguard default   ! Enable globally

